/**
 * Purpose: every call head the engine's catalog publishes, as MeTTa spells
 *   them, so the seat can image them onto its own identifiers at the type
 *   level instead of guessing which heads exist.
 *
 * GENERATED by extensions/python/tools/fngen.py from a fresh running
 * engine's catalog, beside the Python namespace the same tool writes. Edit
 * the catalog and rerun with --write, never edit this file. The `fn-sync`
 * lane fails on any drift.
 *
 * These are the engine's spellings, hyphens and punctuation included. The
 * host spelling of each is `Camel<...>` in naming.ts, which is the SAME rule
 * `tsName` applies at run time; keeping the casing there rather than here is
 * what stops a Python tool deciding how TypeScript spells things.
 */

